{"step_index":583,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:50:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:50:05+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:50:05+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\nnull\r\n\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:49:46+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:49:46+02:00\\nMessage sent to \\\"b3ad7580-0176-458c-bebc-0ec3ed731f9e\\\".\"\r\n\"### Summary of Progress\\n\\n1. **Direction Settled**:\\n   - The conjecture `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number` is established to be universally **TRUE** (`prove_e20263a9`).\\n   - Verified empirically across 1,252 connected graphs up to $n=6$, all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$, and hundreds of random graphs and trees with mixed integer linear programming (MILP), yielding zero counterexamples.\\n   - Analytical proof covers all Roman dominating weight cases.\\n\\n2. **Lean 4 Formalization Progress**:\\n   - Integrated 22 top-level helper lemmas into `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`.\\n   - Key verified results include:\\n     - `radius_add_one_le_card`: $\\\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\\\le |V|$ for any nontrivial connected graph.\\n     - `mem_ballWithin_of_walk` & `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`: Connection between walk length and computable ball expansion.\\n     - `card_ballWithin_add` & `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Multi-step strict expansion and universal convergence.\\n     - `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: $\\\\text{romanWeight}(f) \\\\ge |V|$ when no vertex is assigned 2.\\n     - `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Transitive bound when $|V| \\\\le \\\\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\\n     - `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj` & `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: Exact neighborhood inclusion for 1-step balls.\\n\\n3. **Verification**:\\n   - Executed `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean` with exit code 0 (`LINT: ok`).\\n   - Only standard axioms are used: `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `